libsigrok is a shared library written in C, which is part of the sigrok
signal analysis software suite. It handles the supported devices and
provides a uniform API for the various sigrok frontends.

It supports logic analyzers, oscilloscopes, multimeters, LCR meters,
sound level meters, thermometers, dataloggers, and other types of
measurement devices, connected via USB, serial ports, network, or
Bluetooth.

Sample udev rules for USB device access are installed under
share/examples/libsigrok/ and may need to be copied to the system udev
rules directory on Linux for non-root access to USB devices.
